Resident Execution, Transaction, and Lifecycle Contracts
===============================================================================

This specification consumes primitive observations emitted by the v0.4
resident-runtime observer. It uses the restricted, deterministic
`mech-contract-1` profile so a small Rust reference evaluator and the current
resident Mech evaluator can check the same policy independently.

contract-profile := "mech-contract-1"

1. Resident execution
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`RES-001` requires the case program to use the new production resident route.

-- @requirement RES-001
case-runs-residently! := resident-route === "resident-pure"

`RES-002` requires carried state to survive an explicit resident turn and the
runtime to report exactly that second accepted turn.

-- @requirement RES-002
resident-state-persists! := resident-initial-state === resident-next-turn-state

-- @requirement RES-002
resident-turn-advances! := resident-turns-advanced === true

2. Committed transactions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`TURN-001` requires an explicit commit to be represented by both a durable
transaction record and a semantic commit event.

-- @requirement TURN-001
transaction-commit-outcome! := commit-outcome === "commit"

-- @requirement TURN-001
transaction-commit-recorded! := commit-record-observed === true

-- @requirement TURN-001
transaction-commit-event-recorded! := commit-event-observed === true

`TURN-002` requires transaction-visible mailbox state to become durable after
commit.

-- @requirement TURN-002
transaction-commit-applies-state! := commit-visible-state === commit-after-state

3. Aborted transactions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`TURN-003` requires an explicit abort to emit a semantic abort event.

-- @requirement TURN-003
transaction-abort-outcome! := abort-outcome === "abort"

-- @requirement TURN-003
transaction-abort-event-recorded! := abort-event-observed === true

`TURN-004` is the rollback contract: aborted work must not modify durable
mailbox state.

-- @requirement TURN-004
transaction-abort-preserves-state! := abort-before-state === abort-after-state

4. State and shutdown lifecycle
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`TURN-005` requires committed state to remain visible in the next transaction.

-- @requirement TURN-005
transaction-state-persists! := commit-after-state === next-turn-state

`LIFE-001` requires shutdown to close host-input ingress and publish the
semantic runtime shutdown event.

-- @requirement LIFE-001
shutdown-closes-ingress! := shutdown-ingress-closed === true

-- @requirement LIFE-001
shutdown-rejects-input! := shutdown-input-rejected === true

-- @requirement LIFE-001
shutdown-event-recorded! := shutdown-event-observed === true
